# AUTOPILOT DONE — Onboarding / Company DNA / Readiness Recovery

## 1. ROSA PRE-FLIGHT
Read the onboarding commits (b7f904e, 87db295, 9b99dfa, c73a159, 0070009),
company-dna.ts, company-readiness.ts, onboarding-checkpoints.ts,
SupabaseCompanyDNAStore, RootRoute, ShellGate, CustomerZeroRoute, all
/start /progress /next-question /understanding /confirm /handoff endpoints,
auth boundary, session hydration. No feature work. No Email/Calendar/Drive.
No OnboardingV3/CompanyDNAV2/new state machine — consolidated onto the
readiness architecture the previous sprint introduced.

## 2. PRODUCTION EVIDENCE INSPECTED
- Supabase production: 8 orgs; NONE has a complete DNA record. The
  founder's org (7a9f4986, Gmail connected) has NO DNA row. A new-user org
  (8aae681a) has intake-only DNA (research never completed).
- Railway logs: new-user /start → `customer_zero_started` +
  `research_started`, NO `research_completed` (research threw).
- Deployed commit 0070009 (adoption) at 01:04 UTC; failure evidence after.

## 3. EXISTING-USER LAST_SUCCESSFUL_CHECKPOINT
GET /:org 200 (record branch) — the org's durable state was readable.

## 4. EXISTING-USER FIRST_FAILED_CHECKPOINT
GET /:org 200 response body WITHOUT contextReady/contextMissing/stage —
the Fastify response schema omitted them, so the serializer stripped them.
The portal always saw `contextReady === undefined`.

## 5. EXISTING-USER ROOT_CAUSE
The status response schema (customer-zero.ts) listed only the legacy
fields. `contextReady`, `contextMissing`, `stage` were returned by the
handler but never reached the portal. RootRoute therefore never saw
"ready" → every org was treated as not-ready → CustomerZeroRoute fell
into the LEGACY conversation step → `currentQuestion` returned null →
`buildConversationPayload` emitted the legacy `handoff` →
"Ya tengo suficiente / Vamos a trabajar" (dead: the button's
understanding endpoint had no DNA to show → "No hemos podido preparar el
resumen").

## 6. NEW-USER LAST_SUCCESSFUL_CHECKPOINT
POST /start 200 → `research_started` checkpoint.

## 7. NEW-USER FIRST_FAILED_CHECKPOINT
`research_started` with NO `research_completed` — `fetchAndExtractWebsite`
rejected (unreachable website) → runResearch recorded the RAW Node error
("fetch failed") via failProgress → the portal's ResearchStep showed it
verbatim and the flow reset toward intake.

## 8. NEW-USER ROOT_CAUSE
Unbounded raw error propagation: the web fetch rejection message
("fetch failed") was stored on progress.error and rendered to the CEO.
No business-readable mapping; no retry that preserved the organization.

## 9. WHY LEGACY TERMINAL STILL EXISTED
Two onboarding UIs coexisted: the legacy conversation→handoff step
(next-question returned `handoff` when no question remained) and the new
readiness/understanding path. The portal only entered the new path when
contextMissing === ["confirmation"]; with the schema stripping the stage,
that never happened for pre-DNA orgs.

## 10. WHY "VAMOS A TRABAJAR" WAS DEAD
The button called openConfirmation → api.understanding → the org had no
DNA → nothing to review; the understanding endpoint returned no data and
the flow could not advance.

## 11. WHY UNDERSTANDING RECONSTRUCTION FAILED
Same root cause: stage/contextReady never reached the portal, so it never
routed to the understanding screen, and the org had no DNA to show.

## 12. EXACT CAUSE OF RAW "FETCH FAILED"
Node's undici `fetch` rejects with message "fetch failed" for DNS/TLS/refused
connections. `fetchAndExtractWebsite` did not map it; runResearch recorded
the raw message; ResearchStep rendered `body.error` verbatim.

## 13. CANONICAL STATE MACHINE AFTER FIX
AUTHENTICATED → INTAKE (no DNA) → RESEARCH (intake, research not done) →
DISCOVERY (research done, blocking discovery not done) → UNDERSTANDING
(discovery done, unconfirmed) → READY (confirmed current) → CHAT. The
portal routes exclusively by the durable stage; the legacy handoff
terminal is removed from the API.

## 14. DURABLE RECONSTRUCTION TABLE
FACT | DURABLE SOURCE | WRITER | READER | REQUIRED FOR READINESS
intake | company_dna (company_name, website/description, objective) | /start (projectIntakeToDna) | readinessFactsFromRecord, status | yes
research completion | company_dna.research_completed_at | runResearch (projectResearchToDna) | readinessFactsFromRecord | yes
research facts | company_dna (products, customers, geography, ...) | runResearch / /answer | understanding, readiness | yes
blocking discovery | company_dna.blocking_discovery_completed_at | /answer (markMilestone) | readinessFactsFromRecord | yes
CEO confirmation | company_dna.ceo_confirmed_at (+ facts_updated_at) | /confirm (applyCeoConfirmation) | isConfirmationCurrent | yes
factsUpdatedAt | company_dna.facts_updated_at | all fact writers | isConfirmationCurrent | yes
ceoConfirmedAt | company_dna.ceo_confirmed_at | /confirm | readinessFactsFromRecord | yes
department provisioned | company_dna.department_provisioned_at | /marketing handoff (markMilestone) | readinessFactsFromRecord | yes

## 15. EXISTING-ORG ADOPTION
Existing org without DNA → status 200 stage "intake" on the SAME
organization id (the 404 that wiped the org is gone). Integrations,
conversations and org identity are untouched.

## 16. COMPANY DNA BEHAVIOR
DNA is the single durable source of the five readiness facts. A row alone
is not readiness (L test). Research output is only written when genuine.

## 17. READINESS BEHAVIOR
Evaluated from durable DNA only; never from process memory. The stage is
projected from the same record.

## 18. REFRESH BEHAVIOR
Refresh → status (durable stage) → the portal resumes at the correct
incomplete stage (research/discovery/understanding) or chat when ready.

## 19. BACKEND RESTART BEHAVIOR
Same as refresh — the stage is computed from Supabase; confirmed orgs
return contextReady=true → chat.

## 20. NEW-USER BEHAVIOR
Intake → research (resumable via POST /:org/research on the same org) →
discovery → understanding → confirmation → chat. Research failure shows a
business message + Reintentar; intake is never reset.

## 21. SAFE ERROR UX
web-analysis fetch failures map to "No hemos podido acceder a la web de tu
empresa…". Raw "fetch failed" never reaches the CEO.

## 22. FILES CHANGED
company-readiness.ts (durableOnboardingStage), customer-zero.ts (schema +
404→200 intake + stage), customer-zero-v2.ts (resume research, no handoff),
web-analysis.ts (friendly errors), portal api.ts (stage/research),
CustomerZeroRoute.tsx (stage routing, research retry, no legacy terminal),
CustomerZeroRoute.test.tsx.

